{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b276678dac162bf3","name":"card_event_sneak_attack","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/Breakthrough/events/card_event_sneak_attack","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"SNEAK ATTACK","text":"Destroy target unit. Remove copies of it from the owner's hand and deck.","flavorText":"When the Allies finally gained foothold in the Pacific, the Japanese military forces soon experienced one defeat after another, both on land and sea. After the catastrophic loss at the Battle of Midway 1942 the Japanese Navy never gained its offensive momentum again and both the navy and the army were forced on the defensive. By then many in the Japanese leadership knew the war was lost, but soldiers were ordered to stand their ground, no matter how outnumbered they were, and the strategy was to try to draw as much blood as possible from the Americans in the hopes of drawing them to the negotiation table. By the time the Americans had occupied the islands of Iwo Jima and Okinawa there was a force of  2 million men strong on the Japanese mainland, waiting for the final decisive battle, which never occurred. On August 6 and 9, 1945, the Americans dropped two atomic bombs on the cities of Hiroshima and Nagasaki with such a devastating effect that the Japanese leadership finally decided to surrender to the Allies.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":8,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_sneak_attack","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_sneak_attack_title","SourceString":"SNEAK ATTACK","LocalizedString":"SNEAK ATTACK"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":8,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_sneak_attack_text","SourceString":"Destroy target unit. Remove copies of it from the owner's hand and deck.","LocalizedString":"Destroy target unit. Remove copies of it from the owner's hand and deck."},"fl